 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T07:01+08:00",
 "answer": "**I’d skip an outdoor workout in Jurong right now**, especially running or other strenuous exercise. Singapore’s forecast for **Saturday, October 17** is **PSI 150–230 (unhealthy to very unhealthy)**, and NEA advises even healthy people to avoid prolonged or strenuous outdoor exertion. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nFor an immediate decision, check the **West-region 1-hour PM2.5** reading in NEA’s myENV app; the latest report I found was from **8pm on October 16**, when the West was at **130 µg/m³ (Elevated)**—not a live reading for this moment. If it’s still elevated, avoid strenuous exercise; if it’s high, avoid it altogether. An indoor workout is the safer choice. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
